          "type": "send message",
          "content": "You have attempted this same task before and did not succeed. These are the plans you wrote after those attempts.\nTrial #1: New plan: I got stuck in an infinite loop between the Balcony and the Home office by repeatedly choosing \"north\" and \"south\" without tracking visited rooms. The target room (Sauna) was never reached because I failed to explore the \"west\" direction available in the Balcony. Next time, I will maintain a mental list of visited rooms. Upon entering a room, I will check if I have been there before; if so, I will only try unvisited directions. If all directions lead to visited rooms, I will stop and declare \"DONE\". Specifically, from the Balcony, I should have tried \"west\" first to break the loop.\n\nTrial #2: New plan: I failed to reach the Sauna because I entered a repetitive loop between the Garage, Laundry room, and Bedroom, repeatedly traversing the same edges without ever exploring the \"east\" direction from the Laundry room or the \"east\" direction from the Attic. My strategy lacked a mechanism to track visited rooms and prioritize unexplored directions. Next time, I will maintain a mental set of visited rooms. Upon entering a new room, I will immediately check if I have been there before; if so, I will only attempt directions leading to unvisited rooms. If all available directions lead to visited rooms, I will backtrack to the most recent room with an unexplored direction. Specifically, when in the Laundry room, I must prioritize \"east\" over \"south\" to avoid re-entering the Garage loop, and when in the Attic, I must try \"east\" to find the path to the Sauna.\n\n\nPlease help me with the following task. The goal is to explore rooms and find the target room. In each room, you need to decide the direction to go in. Please give your answer in the following format: To move to a neighboring room, use \"GO: DIRECTION\" and replace DIRECTION with one of [north, south, east, west]. Most importantly, once we have